+// An absent player's character (the user's review: "make sure the disconnected
+// player's area doesn't keep simulating forever"): for 5 minutes after the
+// leave it stays as before (live, vulnerable); then it is parked: it keeps no
+// area online (the ALife switch anchors and the respawn guards skip it), NPCs
+// and monsters do not see it (no STYPE_VISIBLEFORAI; the AI's participant
+// lists skip it), it cannot be hurt (CActor::Hit), its condition and needs
+// stay as they were, and the per-player script passes (the emission's) skip
+// it. It is unparked as it was once its player is back in the world. The
+// clock starts at the leave, or at the server's start for a player who has
+// not joined since.
+const u32 kParkAfterMs = 5 * 60 * 1000;
